<article class="site-article">
  <h1>How WannaWatch works</h1>
  <p class="lede">Same list. Separate phones. One match. Here’s the flow from “I’m bored” to “press play.”</p>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <h2>Start or join a game</h2>
      <p>One person taps Quick play (or Custom game for filters like genre and streaming). Everyone else joins with the six-letter code — or from a friend invite.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Swipe the shared deck</h2>
      <p>Everyone sees the same titles in the same order. Like what you’d watch; pass on the rest. Nobody has to debate out loud until there’s a hit.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h2>Match and watch</h2>
      <p>When the group likes the same title, it’s a match. Open details, check where it’s streaming, and start the movie night you actually agreed on.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <dl class="faq">
    <dt>Do I need an account?</dt>
    <dd>No. You can pick a display name and play right away. Creating a free login lets you restore your profile, friends, and purchases across devices.</dd>

    <dt>Is it only movies?</dt>
    <dd>You can play with movies and TV depending on the game filters. The idea is the same: swipe together until you overlap.</dd>

    <dt>What if nobody matches?</dt>
    <dd>Keep playing for a fresh batch from the same game, or start a new round with different filters.</dd>

    <dt>Are there ads?</dt>
    <dd>Free play may show small banners on home and results, plus a short sponsored pause about every 40 swipes. WannaWatch+ is $2.99/month and removes ads, unlocks Fine-tune, and keeps your full likes and matches history. Cancel anytime.</dd>

    <dt>Is there an iPhone app?</dt>
    <dd>Yes — search WannaWatch on the App Store, or use the web app at <a href="/">wannawatch.app</a> on any device.</dd>
  </dl>

  <p><a class="site-cta" href="/">Play WannaWatch</a> · <a href="/contact">Questions? Contact us</a></p>
</article>
